# Modulus Firmware (ESP-IDF 6.0)

Target **ESP-IDF v6.0** only. Load `esp-idf-6` skill for mechanics; `esp-idf-build` for build/flash.

## MUST

- Use **new driver components** (`esp_driver_*`, `esp_adc`) — legacy `driver/*.h` for ADC/DAC/I2S/GPTimer/PCNT/MCPWM/RMT/tsens **removed in 6.0**.
- Declare `REQUIRES esp_driver_xxx` (or `esp_adc`) in component `CMakeLists.txt`; drop umbrella `driver` dep unless I2C EOL still needed.
- Check every `esp_err_t` return; log with `esp_err_to_name()`; use `ESP_RETURN_ON_ERROR` / `ESP_GOTO_ON_ERROR` / labeled cleanup.
- Use **PSA Crypto** (`psa_*`) for crypto; not legacy `mbedtls_*` primitives. Call `psa_crypto_init()` before crypto if running pre-startup.
- Pull moved components via **`idf_component.yml`**: `espressif/cjson`, `espressif/network_provisioning`, etc.
- Write **warning-clean** C/C++ — default warnings are **errors** (`CONFIG_COMPILER_DISABLE_DEFAULT_ERRORS=n`).
- Assume **Picolibc** default; avoid per-task stdin/stdout/stderr hacks; prefer smaller I/O buffers.

## NEVER

- `#include "driver/adc.h"`, `driver/i2s.h`, `driver/timer.h`, `driver/pcnt.h`, `driver/mcpwm.h`, `driver/rmt.h`, `driver/dac.h`, `driver/temp_sensor.h`.
- `wifi_provisioning` component or `wifi_prov_*` APIs (use registry `network_provisioning` / `network_prov_*`).
- In-tree `cJSON` component path — use `espressif/cjson` from registry.
- Ignore `esp_err_t`. Cast away warnings. Rely on implicit FreeRTOS includes from driver headers.
- `MALLOC_CAP_EXEC` when `CONFIG_ESP_SYSTEM_MEMPROT` enabled (compile error in 6.0).

## Build verify

```powershell
idf.py set-target <chip>
idf.py build
idf.py size
```

Migration guide: https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-idf/en/v6.0/esp32/migration-guides/release-6.x/6.0/index.html
